# The tutorial input lock with windows stacked over each other, and the way back to a
# closed window (docs/LEARNING.md "The input lock", "Getting back"; docs/BUILDING.md
# "Input scripts"). Tutorial 4 at step 5, "Choose a hull", with only Designs open: the
# lesson outlines Create in Designs in the recovery style and says how to open the
# designer again, and offers no Skip meanwhile. Once open, the designer lies over Designs,
# which the step says nothing about: where the designer is, only its Size list responds,
# so its Cancel and Create Design, and Designs' Close under them, are refused.
# layouts: both (also plays at 800x600: run_input_tests.py --small)
options --tutorial=designing-ships:5 --open=designs --layout=1024x768 --size=1280x800

wait-lesson designing-ships
assert-step 5
wait-for item:recovery:designs:create in=lesson
assert-present item:"hint:The * window was closed. Press Create in Designs to open it again." in=lesson
screenshot lesson-lock-windows-reopen
# Long after, still no Skip: the way back is shown instead.
wait 660
assert-present item:Next in=lesson
assert-absent item:Skip in=lesson
# The way back: Create, then Ship.
click tag:designs:create
click item:Ship in=designs
wait-window create-design
wait-gone item:"recovery:*" in=lesson
assert-absent item:"hint:*" in=lesson
# The designer in front: the step's Size list only.
click item:Cancel in=create-design refused
click item:"Create Design" in=create-design refused
click tag:designs:close refused
assert-window create-design
assert-window designs
assert-step 5
screenshot lesson-lock-windows-designer
click item:##size in=create-design
click item:##0 in=create-design
wait-step 6
assert { design_hull_chosen = true }
